# shield/round: the Round shield (P2c ladder slice, LADDER-HEAD; form1, shape1, shape0 legacy round): the hero's first
# shield and the Fjordfolk's. Planks under a leather rim (R: brass from T3), an iron boss (G: a metal-2 boss at T3, a gem
# at T5), the planks' seams (N). At T1 the field is plain unpainted wood (the `shield.t1,!shield.t2` views: the field and
# the device in the wood ramp, one worn spot W); from T2 painted in the field slot, from T3 with its device (a cross from
# the boss in the device slot; the resolver keeps the device off below T3 but for livery).
# Keys (STYLE_P2 25.5; the kite's layout): rest (hangs still on the off arm), guard (raised to the chest; also the hurt
# hold), block (squared to the threat, a size up, a glint on the rim's top-left: the delight), lie (flat on the ground
# beside the corpse: `anchor pivot`, laid level under the turned body), back (slung for seated and kneeling postures).
# Layers: facing down and left the face is in front; facing up its back (boards, strap, buckle) behind the arm; facing
# right its back behind the body, raised edge-on before the chest (layer neck) for guard and block. Regions (contracts
# 3b): R the rim, P the field round the device, G the boss, N the boards, W wear. Written by the LADDER-HEAD area's
# gen_shields.py from shape masks and checked by eye at 1x and 8x. Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# (LADDER-HEAD i3, w3/gen_round3.py) T2: a brass rim, the accent field with a tan cross through the boss (a painted
# shield; T1 keeps bare boards)
use person
body adult
role shield form1
role shield shape1
role shield shape0
layer shield
anchor gripL
keys shield
tags overlay
legend R field 1
legend S field 2
legend T field 3
legend F device 2
legend J device 3

